---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy">
  <article class="container py-16 max-w-4xl">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-heading font-bold mb-4">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="text-slate-600">Updated 22 November 2026</p>

    <h2>Who is responsible?</h2>
    <p>Rufus Plaga, Im Fischergarten 1, 88250 Weingarten, Germany, is the controller for this portfolio.
      You can contact me about your data at <a href="mailto:plagarufus@gmail.com">plagarufus@gmail.com</a>.</p>

    <h2>When you visit</h2>
    <p>GitHub Pages hosts the portfolio, including its fonts, videos and animation scripts.
      Your browser sends GitHub the requested file and connection information so it can deliver the page.
      GitHub logs visitors’ IP addresses for security. My legal basis is my legitimate interest in operating
      a reliable, secure website under Article 6(1)(f) GDPR. GitHub determines retention according to
      operational, security and legal needs. See the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub privacy statement</a>.</p>
    <p>GoDaddy provides the domain’s DNS service. When a DNS resolver looks up this domain, GoDaddy may receive the requested
      domain and the resolver’s IP address to return the server address. I use this service to make the portfolio reachable
      under its domain under Article 6(1)(f) GDPR. GoDaddy explains its retention criteria and international transfers
      in its <a href="https://www.godaddy.com/legal/agreements/privacy-policy">privacy notice</a>.</p>

    <h2>Your cookie choice</h2>
    <p>You can use the full portfolio with analytics declined. This site stores your choice as “accepted” or “declined”,
      the date and time of the choice, and the version of the consent notice under <code>cookieConsent</code> in your
      browser’s local storage. It stays there until you change it or your browser clears site data. If the notice changes,
      we ask you again before loading analytics. This storage is necessary to respect your choice under § 25(2) no. 2 TDDDG.
      My legitimate interest in remembering that choice is the basis under Article 6(1)(f) GDPR.</p>

    <h2 id="analytics">Optional Google Analytics</h2>
    <p>If you accept analytics, Google Ireland Limited receives information about the pages you visit, time spent,
      referral source, browser and device. Where detailed location and device collection is enabled, this can include the
      approximate city, device model, browser version and screen resolution. I use these reports to understand which projects
      interest visitors and improve the portfolio.
      For traffic from the EU, Switzerland and the UK, Google uses the IP address to derive an approximate location and
      discards it before logging the analytics data. See <a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/12017362">Google’s regional data handling</a>.</p>
    <p>Google uses first-party cookies such as <code>_ga</code> to distinguish browsers and
      <code>_ga_YMVG11GXL5</code> to remember a session. Google documents a default lifetime of two years for these cookies.
      Browser limits can shorten it. Your consent is the basis for storing and reading analytics cookies under § 25(1) TDDDG
      and for processing personal data under Article 6(1)(a) GDPR.</p>
    <p>For this portfolio, Google Analytics is set to retain event data for 2 months and user data for 14 months.
      Each new event associated with your user identifier restarts the 14-month period for that identifier.
      These settings do not affect standard aggregated reports.
      See <a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/7667196">Google’s explanation of retention</a>.</p>
    <p>Open Cookie Settings and select “Decline analytics” to withdraw. The site stops analytics collection and clears
      its analytics cookies from this browser. Withdrawal applies going forward. You can contact me about data already processed.</p>
    <button type="button" onclick="window.openCookieSettings()" class="border-2 border-slate-600 rounded-full px-5 py-2 hover:bg-slate-100">Cookie Settings</button>

    <h2>International transfers</h2>
    <p>These providers may process information in the United States. For covered transfers to certified US recipients,
      the EU–US Data Privacy Framework provides an adequacy basis. For other transfers providers may use the European Commission’s
      standard contractual clauses. Details of the applicable safeguards are in the hosting and DNS notices above and in
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy/frameworks">Google’s transfer policy</a>. You can contact me for a copy of the relevant safeguards.</p>

    <h2>If you email me</h2>
    <p>I use Gmail to receive and reply to your message. I process your email address, the contents of your message and
      any attachments to respond to you. For a request about a possible contract, the basis is Article 6(1)(b) GDPR.
      For other inquiries, my legitimate interest in responding is the basis under Article 6(1)(f).
      I keep correspondence while needed for the inquiry and for any applicable statutory retention period.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>You can ask me for access, correction, deletion, restriction or portability of your personal data where applicable.
      You can object to processing based on legitimate interests for reasons relating to your particular situation.
      To exercise these rights, email <a href="mailto:plagarufus@gmail.com">plagarufus@gmail.com</a>.</p>
    <p>You may also lodge a complaint with a data protection authority, including the authority where you live, work or believe
      an infringement occurred. My local authority is the
      <a href="https://www.baden-wuerttemberg.datenschutz.de/beschwerde/">Baden-Württemberg Commissioner for Data Protection and Freedom of Information</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  h2 { @apply text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3; }
  p { @apply mb-4; }
  a { @apply underline text-red-700; }
  #analytics { scroll-margin-top: 6rem; }
</style>
